Subject: [PATCH] Charge deposition: keep normalized coords and shape factors in double

Applies the single-precision hardening that current deposition already has, to the
charge deposition path that was missed.

THE ASYMMETRY. Source/Particles/Deposition/CurrentDeposition.H computes the normalized
particle coordinate and the shape factors in double, and converts back to amrex::Real
only for the final scatter. It carries the in-source comment "Keep these double to avoid
bug in single precision" (lines ~115, ~127). The structurally identical code in
ChargeDeposition.H does all of that work in amrex::Real, which is binary32 in a
single-precision build.

WHY IT SHOWS UP IN rho AND NOT IN j. A normalized coordinate on a 1024-cell axis is
O(1e3); converting it to binary32 before index/weight selection discards far more than
one field-scale ulp, so platforms whose FMA/instruction selection differs can choose
slightly different shape weights. Same-species currents ADD, so that error stays at
round-off. Total charge density is the NEAR-CANCELLING difference of two same-magnitude
species densities, and the cancellation amplifies the relative error enormously.

MEASURED (two-species Langmuir, 1024^2, PPC1, single precision, Yee FDTD, identical
decks/seeds, two platforms compared at step 1):
    Ex, Ez, jx, jz   max|d|/RMS ~ 6e-5, rel-L2 ~ 1.1e-5   (round-off)
    particle counts  exact, both species
    rho              max|d|/RMS ~ 1.8e-1, rel-L2 ~ 2.2e-2
Normalizing the same rho difference against a SINGLE species density (3.204e5 C/m^3)
instead of the near-cancelled net gives 2.24e-6 RMS / 1.90e-5 max -- i.e. the underlying
deposition error really is round-off scale, and the reported 2% is cancellation
amplifying it.

WHY IT IS EASY TO MISS. Particle counts and field-energy invariants pass cleanly; only
the deposited charge is wrong. A count-based sanity check sees a healthy run.

IMPACT. Under plain Yee FDTD rho is diagnostic-only, so this corrupts charge-density,
Gauss-law and charge-conservation DIAGNOSTICS without affecting the evolution. It becomes
PHYSICS-ACTIVE wherever rho is consumed: electrostatic solvers, HybridPIC, div-E cleaning,
and rho-corrected PSATD. Double-precision builds are unaffected.

THE CHANGE. Mirror CurrentDeposition exactly: compute the normalized coordinate and the
shape factors in double, then convert to amrex::Real immediately before the deposition
loop, leaving the loop itself untouched. Applied to both doChargeDepositionShapeN and
doChargeDepositionSharedShapeN, and to every geometry variant (Cartesian, RZ, RCYLINDER,
RSPHERE).

*** NOT YET VALIDATED ON HARDWARE *** -- authored while the GPU/SP build hosts were
unreachable. Before landing: rebuild SP, re-run the field-level comparison, and confirm
rho falls to round-off parity alongside Ex/Ez/jx/jz. Generated against WarpX
87fb74da702088687725c5e6458cc0e8fa2953a5.

